*
* Component: Source_Maxwell_direct
*
* %I
* Written by: Adrian Merritt (TAVI project)
* Date: October 16, 2026
* Version: 1.0
* Origin: TAVI
* Release: McStas 3.x
*
* Rectangular neutron source with a facility spectrum of up to three Maxwellians,
* sampled directly in energy: every ray leaves with the same weight.
*
* %D
* A rectangular neutron source that emits into a rectangular angular window and
* has one of two modes, chosen by the setting parameter flat_band.
*
* Full spectrum (flat_band=0, the default). The flux spectrum is the sum of up
* to three Maxwellians, exactly the one Source_gen builds from the same T1..T3,
* I1..I3 (P. Ageron, Nucl. Inst. Meth. A 284 (1989) 197). In wavelength each
* Maxwellian is normalised to one,
*   SG(L,T) = 2 a^2 exp(-a/L^2) / L^5,  a = 949/T  (T in K, L in Angstrom),
* and the flux per steradian, cm^2 and second is the sum of Ii*SG(L,Ti). In
* energy, with E = C/L^2 and C = VS2E*K2V^2*4*PI^2 (about 81.80 meV Angstrom^2),
* the same kernel is the density E exp(-E/th)/th^2 with th = C*T/949 meV, a
* Gamma(2,th) distribution. The component draws E from it directly: it picks
* one active pair i with probability Ii/sum(I) and sets E = -th_i ln(U1 U2). A
* pair is active when T>0 and I>0. There are no energy or wavelength cut-offs:
* the source emits over the whole spectrum, however far the tails reach.
*
* Flat band (flat_band=1). E is uniform in [E0-dE, E0+dE] and the facility
* spectrum (T1..I3) plays no part in the sampling or the weight, though T1..I3
* must still be valid.
* This mode is deliberately unphysical. It exists to get good statistics around
* one energy quickly, and its total intensity scales with dE: flux is the
* intensity per energy unit, n/cm^2/s/sr/meV, and is arbitrary (default 1).
* Do not compare its absolute intensity with the full spectrum.
*
* Emission geometry. The position is uniform on the rectangle in the z=0 plane
* and t=0. The direction is drawn with randvec_target_rect_angular, as Source_gen
* does, uniform per steradian in a window focus_aw wide (horizontal) and focus_ah
* high (vertical), both full widths, centred on the z axis. The window has the
* solid angle Omega = 2*focus_aw*sin(focus_ah/2) (radians). The window is a
* latitude/longitude rectangle: the horizontal angle is uniform in
* +-focus_aw/2 and the vertical angle is asin(U*sin(focus_ah/2)); focus_ah must
* not exceed 180 deg and focus_aw must not exceed 360 deg.
*
* One weight. Every ray leaves with the same weight, set in INITIALIZE:
*   full spectrum: p = sum(Ii) * 1e4 * xwidth * yheight * Omega / ncount
*   flat band:     p = flux * 2*dE * 1e4 * xwidth * yheight * Omega / ncount
* (the sum runs over the active pairs; the 1e4 turns m^2 into cm^2). The source
* never reweights a ray by its energy, direction or position, so a downstream
* histogram of rays shows the spectrum, not a weighted sample of a flat one.
*
* No guides. The spectrum is the moderator's, at the source plane. Place guides,
* windows and filters after this component to model what a real beam line adds.
*
* Invalid input stops the run. INITIALIZE prints a message that names the
* component, its instance and the parameter with its value on stderr, then
* exits. It refuses a non-positive xwidth, yheight, focus_aw or focus_ah, a
* window beyond 360 x 180 deg, any T or I that is negative or not finite, an
* input with no active pair, an I sum that overflows, an active pair whose
* energy scale is not finite, a ray weight that is not
* finite or not positive, a flat_band other than 0 or 1, and, with
* flat_band=1, a dE or flux that is not positive or an E0-dE that is not
* positive. In full-spectrum mode E0, dE and flux are neither read nor checked.
*
* Switching flat_band at run time (for example from an instrument parameter)
* does not need a recompile.
*
* Version. The Version line in %I is the component's version number. A change to
* the physics, to the weight or to the parameters is a version change.
*
* Facility parameters (the table of Source_gen, copied unchanged; every row
* works here, all use T1..T3 and I1..I3). Source_Maxwell_direct is rectangular
* only: the HZB cold row names a radius, which this component does not take, so
* give xwidth and yheight instead.
*
* PSI cold source     T1=296.2,I1=8.5E11, T2=40.68,I2=5.2E11
* ILL VCS cold source T1=216.8,I1=1.24e+13,T2=33.9,I2=1.02e+13
*        (H1, 58 MW)  T3=16.7 ,I3=3.0423e+12
* ILL HCS cold source T1=413.5,I1=10.22e12,T2=145.8,I2=3.44e13
*        (H5, 58 MW)  T3=40.1 ,I3=2.78e13
* ILL Thermal tube    T1=683.7,I1=0.5874e+13,T2=257.7,I2=2.5099e+13
*        (H12, 58 MW) T3=16.7 ,I3=1.0343e+12
* ILL Hot source      T1=1695, I1=1.74e13,T2=708,  I2=3.9e12 (58MW)
* HZB cold source     T1=43.7 ,I1=1.4e12, T2=137.2,I2=2.08e12,radius=.155 (10MW)
* HZB bi-spectral     T1=43.7, I1=1.4e12, T2=137.2,I2=2.08e12,T3=293.0,I3=1.77e12
* HZB thermal tube    T1=293.0,I1=2.64e12 (10MW)
* FRM2 cold,20MW      T1=35.0, I1=9.38e12,T2=547.5,I2=2.23e12,T3=195.4,I3=1.26e13
* FRM2 thermal,20MW   T1=285.6,I1=3.06e13,T2=300.0,I2=1.68e12,T3=429.9,I3=6.77e12
* LLB cold,14MW       T1=220,  I1=2.09e12,T2=60,   I2=3.83e12,T3=20,   I3=1.04e12
* TRIGA thermal 1MW   T1=300,  I1=3.5e11 (scale by thermal power in MW)
*
* Usage example:
*   Source_Maxwell_direct(xwidth=0.1, yheight=0.1, focus_aw=2, focus_ah=2,
*     T1=285.6, I1=3.06e13, T2=300.0, I2=1.68e12, T3=429.9, I3=6.77e12)
*   Source_Maxwell_direct(xwidth=0.1, yheight=0.1, focus_aw=2, focus_ah=2,
*     T1=300, I1=1e13, flat_band=1, E0=14.7, dE=2)
*
* %VALIDATION
* 2026-10-16, McStas 3.7.1 (git) with MSVC, by tools/verify_source_maxwell_direct.py
* in the TAVI repository, against Source_gen. Run that tool before any change to
* this component (about 15 s; it compiles Test_Source_Maxwell_direct and checks the
* monitors' I, I_err and N). Fixed seeds, so a rerun gives the same numbers. Every
* check below passed. Ray counts: 2e7 per facility row and source, 5e6 for the flat
* band and the wide window, 1e6 for the E0/dE comparison.
* 1. Spectrum equals Source_gen's: all 12 Source_gen facility rows and a single
*    temperature (300 K, 1e13), in the wavelength and the energy monitor (500 bins,
*    bins wholly inside the range Source_gen samples, N>=20 in both). chi2/n from
*    0.87 to 1.11 over 26 comparisons, at least 276 bins each, every chi2 inside
*    n +- 4 sqrt(2n). Control: the FRM2 thermal row with I2 doubled gives chi2 6786
*    (500 bins) and 6693 (365 bins) and fails the band, as it must. The %D table
*    matches Source_gen's labels, order and numbers.
* 2. Absolute total in [Lmin, Lmax] equals the analytic sum of Ii times the
*    Gamma(2) mass in range, times 1e4*xwidth*yheight*Omega: 26 totals (both
*    sources), the largest deviation 1.26 sigma.
* 3. One weight: I/N equals the predicted weight to 5e-10 and I_err^2*N equals I^2
*    to 2e-9 in every non-empty bin of the wavelength, energy, position and
*    divergence monitors (tolerance 1e-4), full spectrum and flat band. Control:
*    Source_gen's own output fails the same test.
* 4. Full spectrum ignores E0 and dE: four runs with other E0 and dE give monitor
*    arrays bit-identical to the baseline; a different seed differs.
* 5. Flat band: no counts outside [E0-dE, E0+dE]; intensity per meV equals
*    flux*1e4*xwidth*yheight*Omega (ratio 1.000000 in two settings); uniform in
*    energy (chi2 69.5 for 60 bins, 104.4 for 100 bins).
* 6. Refusals: T1<0, I1<0, T2=nan, no active pair (T=0 and I=0), flat band with
*    E0<=dE, dE=0, flux=0, flat_band=2, focus_aw=0 and focus_ah=181 each stop the
*    run with a message naming the parameter; the same E0 and dE are accepted in
*    full-spectrum mode. The I-sum and ray-weight overflow refusals were checked by
*    hand on the test instrument, not by the tool.
* 7. Uniform per steradian: a 60 x 120 deg window, 5e6 rays. The vertical angle as
*    McStas's Divergence_monitor measures it, atan2(vy,vz), matches the exact
*    per-steradian expectation (chi2 95.2, 128 bins, band 64..192) and fails the
*    expectation of a sampler uniform in angle (chi2 117325) and of one uniform in
*    latitude (chi2 167130). The horizontal angle is uniform (chi2 123.8, 120 bins).
* Resolution: an energy-scale error as small as 0.04 percent (kT instead of
* C*T/949) is not detected.
*
* %P
* xwidth: [m]           Width of the source
* yheight: [m]          Height of the source
* focus_aw: [deg]       Full horizontal width of the emission window (uniform per steradian)
* focus_ah: [deg]       Full vertical height of the emission window (uniform per steradian)
* T1: [K]               Temperature of the first Maxwellian
* I1: [1/(s*cm**2*sr)]  Integrated flux per solid angle and area of the first Maxwellian
* T2: [K]               Temperature of the second Maxwellian, 0=none
* I2: [1/(s*cm**2*sr)]  Integrated flux of the second Maxwellian, 0=none
* T3: [K]               Temperature of the third Maxwellian, 0=none
* I3: [1/(s*cm**2*sr)]  Integrated flux of the third Maxwellian, 0=none
* flat_band: [0|1]      0: full spectrum (default), 1: unphysical flat band in energy
* E0: [meV]             Flat band: centre energy (read only when flat_band=1)
* dE: [meV]             Flat band: half width (read only when flat_band=1)
* flux: [1/(s*cm**2*sr*meV)]  Flat band: flux per energy unit (read only when flat_band=1)
*
* %L
* Source_gen, McStas component library (the spectrum and facility table).
* P. Ageron, Nucl. Inst. Meth. A 284 (1989) 197
*
* %E
*******************************************************************************/

DEFINE COMPONENT Source_Maxwell_direct

SETTING PARAMETERS (xwidth, yheight, focus_aw, focus_ah, T1, I1, T2=0, I2=0,
                    T3=0, I3=0, int flat_band=0, E0=0, dE=0, flux=1)

/* Neutron parameters: (x,y,z,vx,vy,vz,t,sx,sy,sz,p) */

SHARE
%{
#ifndef SOURCE_MAXWELL_DIRECT_DEF
#define SOURCE_MAXWELL_DIRECT_DEF
  /* Report one refused parameter and stop. Only INITIALIZE calls it. */
  void smd_refuse(const char *comp, const char *param, double value, const char *rule)
  {
    fprintf(stderr, "Source_Maxwell_direct: %s: %s=%g %s\n", comp, param, value, rule);
    exit(-1);
  }
#endif
%}

DECLARE
%{
  double pair_theta[3]; /* energy scale of each active pair [meV] */
  double pair_cum[3];   /* cumulative selection probability over the active pairs */
  int    n_pairs;       /* number of active pairs */
  double dist;          /* distance to the next component [m], 0 if none; display only */
  double p_ray;         /* the one weight of every ray */
%}

INITIALIZE
%{
  double Tv[3], Iv[3];
  double sumI = 0, omega_sr, c_e;
  int k;
  static const char *tname[3] = {"T1", "T2", "T3"};

  Tv[0] = T1; Tv[1] = T2; Tv[2] = T3;
  Iv[0] = I1; Iv[1] = I2; Iv[2] = I3;

  if (!(isfinite(xwidth)   && xwidth   > 0)) smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, "xwidth",   xwidth,   "must be finite and > 0");
  if (!(isfinite(yheight)  && yheight  > 0)) smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, "yheight",  yheight,  "must be finite and > 0");
  if (!(isfinite(focus_aw) && focus_aw > 0 && focus_aw <= 360))
    smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, "focus_aw", focus_aw, "must be finite, > 0 and <= 360 deg");
  if (!(isfinite(focus_ah) && focus_ah > 0 && focus_ah <= 180))
    smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, "focus_ah", focus_ah, "must be finite, > 0 and <= 180 deg");
  if (flat_band != 0 && flat_band != 1) smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, "flat_band", flat_band, "must be 0 (full spectrum) or 1 (flat band)");

  for (k = 0; k < 3; k++) {
    static const char *iname[3] = {"I1", "I2", "I3"};
    if (!(isfinite(Tv[k]) && Tv[k] >= 0)) smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, tname[k], Tv[k], "must be finite and >= 0");
    if (!(isfinite(Iv[k]) && Iv[k] >= 0)) smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, iname[k], Iv[k], "must be finite and >= 0");
  }

  /* active pairs: T>0 and I>0, kept in order; the selection probability is I/sum(I) */
  c_e = VS2E*K2V*K2V*4*PI*PI; /* E = c_e/L^2, the same constant Source_gen's kernel implies */
  n_pairs = 0;
  for (k = 0; k < 3; k++) {
    if (Tv[k] > 0 && Iv[k] > 0) {
      pair_theta[n_pairs] = c_e*Tv[k]/949.0;
      if (!isfinite(pair_theta[n_pairs])) smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, tname[k], Tv[k], "gives an energy scale that is not finite");
      pair_cum[n_pairs]   = Iv[k];
      sumI += Iv[k];
      n_pairs++;
    }
  }
  if (!isfinite(sumI)) {
    fprintf(stderr, "Source_Maxwell_direct: %s: I1=%g I2=%g I3=%g: their sum overflows\n", NAME_CURRENT_COMP, I1, I2, I3);
    exit(-1);
  }
  if (n_pairs == 0) {
    fprintf(stderr, "Source_Maxwell_direct: %s: T1=%g I1=%g T2=%g I2=%g T3=%g I3=%g: no pair has T>0 and I>0\n",
            NAME_CURRENT_COMP, T1, I1, T2, I2, T3, I3);
    exit(-1);
  }
  for (k = 0; k < n_pairs; k++) pair_cum[k] = (k ? pair_cum[k-1] : 0) + pair_cum[k]/sumI;
  pair_cum[n_pairs-1] = 1.0; /* no rounding gap at the top */

  if (flat_band) {
    if (!(isfinite(dE)   && dE   > 0)) smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, "dE",   dE,   "must be finite and > 0 in flat-band mode");
    if (!(isfinite(E0)))               smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, "E0",   E0,   "must be finite in flat-band mode");
    if (!(E0 - dE > 0)) {
      fprintf(stderr, "Source_Maxwell_direct: %s: E0=%g dE=%g: the flat band must have E0 - dE > 0\n", NAME_CURRENT_COMP, E0, dE);
      exit(-1);
    }
    if (!(isfinite(flux) && flux > 0)) smd_refuse(NAME_CURRENT_COMP, "flux", flux, "must be finite and > 0 in flat-band mode");
  }

  /* the one weight; Omega is the solid angle of the emission window */
  omega_sr = 2*focus_aw*DEG2RAD*sin(focus_ah*DEG2RAD/2);
  if (flat_band)
    p_ray = flux*2*dE*1e4*xwidth*yheight*omega_sr/mcget_ncount();
  else
    p_ray = sumI*1e4*xwidth*yheight*omega_sr/mcget_ncount();
  if (!(isfinite(p_ray) && p_ray > 0)) {
    fprintf(stderr, "Source_Maxwell_direct: %s: ray weight %g is not finite and > 0 (I1..I3 sum %g, xwidth=%g, yheight=%g, focus_aw=%g, focus_ah=%g; flat band also flux, dE)\n",
            NAME_CURRENT_COMP, p_ray, sumI, xwidth, yheight, focus_aw, focus_ah);
    exit(-1);
  }

  /* distance to the next component, for the display only */
  dist = 0;
  if (INDEX_CURRENT_COMP < mcNUMCOMP) { /* component indices run 1..mcNUMCOMP */
    Coords ToTarget;
    double tx, ty, tz;
    ToTarget = coords_sub(POS_A_COMP_INDEX(INDEX_CURRENT_COMP+1), POS_A_CURRENT_COMP);
    ToTarget = rot_apply(ROT_A_CURRENT_COMP, ToTarget);
    coords_get(ToTarget, &tx, &ty, &tz);
    dist = sqrt(tx*tx + ty*ty + tz*tz);
  }
%}

TRACE
%{
  double E, v, u, u1, u2, nrm, solid_angle;
  int k;

  /* position: uniform on the rectangle */
  x = randpm1()*xwidth/2;
  y = randpm1()*yheight/2;
  z = 0;
  t = 0;

  /* energy */
  if (flat_band) {
    E = E0 + dE*randpm1();
  } else {
    u = rand01();
    for (k = 0; k < n_pairs - 1; k++)
      if (u < pair_cum[k]) break; /* u==1 or rounding falls to the last active pair */
    do { /* rand01 can return exactly 0 (log) or 1 (E=0): redraw */
      u1 = rand01();
      u2 = rand01();
    } while (u1 <= 0 || u2 <= 0 || u1*u2 >= 1);
    E = -pair_theta[k]*log(u1*u2);
  }

  /* direction: uniform per steradian in the window, speed from E */
  randvec_target_rect_angular(&vx, &vy, &vz, &solid_angle, 0, 0, 1,
                              focus_aw*DEG2RAD, focus_ah*DEG2RAD, ROT_A_CURRENT_COMP);
  nrm = sqrt(vx*vx + vy*vy + vz*vz);
  v = SE2V*sqrt(E)/nrm;
  vx *= v; vy *= v; vz *= v;

  p = p_ray; /* the only assignment to p */

  SCATTER;
%}

MCDISPLAY
%{
  multiline(5, -xwidth/2.0, -yheight/2.0, 0.0,
                xwidth/2.0, -yheight/2.0, 0.0,
                xwidth/2.0,  yheight/2.0, 0.0,
               -xwidth/2.0,  yheight/2.0, 0.0,
               -xwidth/2.0, -yheight/2.0, 0.0);
  /* tan(focus_aw/2) diverges at 180 deg and flips sign beyond, so no dashed window there */
  if (dist && focus_aw < 180) { /* the dashed window needs a next component to reach */
    double hw = dist*tan(focus_aw*DEG2RAD/2);
    double hh = dist*tan(focus_ah*DEG2RAD/2)/cos(focus_aw*DEG2RAD/2); /* latitude/longitude corner */
    dashed_line(0,0,0, -hw,-hh,dist, 4);
    dashed_line(0,0,0,  hw,-hh,dist, 4);
    dashed_line(0,0,0,  hw, hh,dist, 4);
    dashed_line(0,0,0, -hw, hh,dist, 4);
  }
%}

END
